0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#what-execution-buys-you","title":"What execution buys you"},{"depth":2,"url":"#whats-new-in-the-deployment","title":"What's new in the deployment"},{"depth":2,"url":"#whats-new-in-the-build-invocation","title":"What's new in the build invocation"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-stays-exactly-the-same","title":"What stays exactly the same"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-to-expect-the-first-time","title":"What to expect the first time"},{"depth":2,"url":"#faq","title":"FAQ"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"From cache to execution"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"You have a cache serving hits. This is what changes when the misses stop running on your laptop: in the deployment, in the build invocation, and in what breaks first."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone who finished Getting started and is deciding whether to\ntake the next step. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," an accurate picture of\nwhat remote execution adds, what it costs, and which wall you'll hit first.\n",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," ten minutes of reading, no commands."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["A cache serving hits to your build. If you don't have one yet, start with ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/getting-started","children":"Getting started"}],"."]}]}]]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["A cache answers exactly one question: ",["$","em",null,{"children":"has this exact action already been\nrun somewhere?"}]," When the answer is yes, you get the result back in\nmilliseconds. When the answer is no (and on a first build, or after a\ntoolchain bump, the answer is no for almost everything) something still has\nto run the action. With caching alone, that something is the machine you're\nsitting at."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Remote execution changes the answer to that second question. The misses go\nto a fleet."}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"what-execution-buys-you","children":"What execution buys you"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Two things, and it's worth being clear that they're separate."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"The misses stop being your problem."}]," A cache makes repeated work free; it\ndoes nothing for work nobody has done yet. A clean build, a dependency bump,\na merge that invalidates half the graph: these are all cache misses by\ndefinition, and they are exactly the builds that hurt. Remote execution is\nwhat turns those into a fan-out across as many cores as you're willing to\npay for, instead of a fan-out across the eight your laptop has."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Actions get to run on hardware that fits them."}]," Once a scheduler is\nrouting work, actions stop being homogeneous. A link step that needs 64 GB\nof RAM, a test that needs a GPU, a cross-compile that needs a specific libc:\neach can be routed to a worker that has it, without every developer\nneeding that machine under their desk. This is the part that has no local\nequivalent at all, and for some teams it's the whole reason to adopt\nForge."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["A third thing people expect and don't get: remote execution is not\nautomatically ",["$","em",null,{"children":"faster"}]," per action. A single action that takes 200 ms locally\nwill take 200 ms plus a network round-trip plus input materialization\nremotely. The win is parallelism and placement, not per-action latency,\nwhich is why ","$L8","\ncovers keeping small actions local."]}],"\n","$L9","\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22"]}],"$L23"]}],["$L24","$L25"],"$L26"]}],"isPartial":"$@27","staleTime":"$28","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L29","isPartial":"$@2a","staleTime":"$28","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L2b","isPartial":"$@2c","staleTime":"$28","varyParams":"$2d"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@2e","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@2f"}
